refireSkipsDegraded -- A REFIRE SILENTLY SKIPS EVERY STATEMENT THAT DEGRADED AT COMPILE.

Minted 2026-09-25 by Tony's dispatch (the per-kind += follow-ups: "a refire must never
silently return a stale value; if it is general, bank it as a fixit citizen").

THE MECHANISM. A construct with no emitter degrades: jitDegrade announces it and the
construct RUNS AT EMIT TIME, once, while the function is being built. The compiled
function does not contain it. So a refire runs the compiled code WITHOUT it. Two shapes:
  alone      nothing else emitted, so nothing is compiled; jitRefire prints NOTHING
             COMPILED YET and runs nothing at all, and the caller reads whatever the
             fields held before.
  beside a   the sibling compiles and runs per fire; the degraded construct ran once at
  sibling    emit and never again. This file is that shape: rsN goes 1 then 2 while
             RS SINK FIRED prints once where the interpreted road prints it twice.

THE COUNT, measured 2026-09-25 over the degrading constructs with an observable effect,
each alone and beside a sibling, compiled once and refired:
  cerr     degrades; runs at emit only, in both shapes              SKIPPED ON REFIRE
  search   degrades; runs at emit only, in both shapes              SKIPPED ON REFIRE
           (the effect is invisible there; the count of fires is not)
  FOR      degrades BY NAME, yet the refire DOES run it -- jmF 2 then 4, correct
  +=       was the fourth, until the run-time call-through: J2 read 4 then 4 where the
           interpreted road read 4 then 10. Fixed 2026-09-25, and the reason this was asked.
  a string expression row was VOID -- the probe's own spelling failed to parse on the
  interpreted road too -- and is not graded.
So it is GENERAL: two of the three measured degrading constructs are skipped on refire,
and FOR shows that a degrade line alone does not say which kind a construct is. That is
the 2026-08-08 rule collecting again: a degrade asserts that a fallback OCCURRED, never
that it was sound.

NEXT: OPEN -- the fix is not chosen, and it is Tony's. What would generate a candidate:
